 Ford, And More", "url": "https://www.motor1.com/news/594953/fastest-cars-goodwood-festival-of-speed/"}, {"title": "WORDS: ELLIOTT HUGHES | PHOTOGRAPHY: GOODWOOD", "url": "https://www.magnetomagazine.com/?p=21296"}, {"title": "McMurtry Spéirling Smashes Goodwood Hillclimb Record", "url": "https://jalopnik.com/mcmurtry-speirling-smashes-goodwood-hillclimb-record-1849111501"}, {"title": "10 Fastest Cars At The 2022 Goodwood FoS: Porsche, Ford, And More", "url": "https://www.motor1.com/news/594953/fastest-cars-goodwood-festival-of-speed/about:blank"}, {"title": "McMurtry Spéirling sets OUTRIGHT HILLCLIMB RECORD at Goodwood Festival of Speed", "url": "https://mcmurtry.com/?p=25590"}, {"title": "Electric vehicles (EVs) dominate at Goodwood Festival of Speed’s Hill Climb event", "url": "https://electricdrives.tv/electric-vehicles-evs-dominate-at-goodwood-festival-of-speeds-hill-climb-event/"}, {"title": "Electric vehicles (EVs) dominate at Goodwood Festival of Speed’s Hill Climb event", "url": "https://electricdrives.tv/?p=9924"}]}, "The search confirms the core claim: Max Chilton set a 39.08-second hillclimb record at the 2022 Goodwood Festival of Speed in the electric McMurtry Spéirling.\n\n- **The run:** Chilton's time smashed the 41.60-second marker set by Nick Heidfeld back in 1999 behind the wheel of a McLaren MP4/13 F1 car. Sources differ on the year of Heidfeld's run; one says 1998 McLaren MP4/13 during the 1999 Festival of Speed.\n- **Previous electric benchmark:** Romain Dumas's Volkswagen ID.R set a 39.90-second lap in 2019, but it remained an unofficial record due to it being achieved in qualifying. Chilton's run beat that time by 0.82s.\n- **Official status:** Jalopnik notes that Formula One cars can no longer make timed competitive runs up the hill climb for safety reasons. The McMurtry team claims the result sets both official and unofficial hill records, though that is the manufacturer's own framing.\n- **Car specs:** One source reports the car has nearly 1,000 horsepower, and another describes it as unveiled at the Goodwood Festival of Speed 2021 as a demonstrator before the record attempt.\n- **Field:** Per Motor1's top-10 list, the Spéirling took first, ahead of a Porsche 718 GT4 ePerformance at 45.50 seconds, and four electric vehicles placed in the top 10."], "durationSeconds": 6.873747582999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_015wY9PaBTiKSDSfBujkCFgh", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
